WEBVTT

00:11.553 --> 00:14.305
MOSH PIT

00:16.391 --> 00:19.227
Why are they here?

00:22.272 --> 00:23.815
What? En?

00:24.649 --> 00:27.318
No way. You're still alive?

00:27.402 --> 00:30.947
You pieces of shit,
stop acting like you don't know!

00:31.031 --> 00:34.826
You killed En
and took his head, didn't you?!

00:34.909 --> 00:38.288
En is dead. That's a doll.

00:38.371 --> 00:41.666
A tool that's leading us to the real one.

00:45.795 --> 00:49.591
I see. So the head is in that room.

00:49.674 --> 00:53.053
Does that mean
the Cross-Eyes' boss is also inside?

00:54.054 --> 00:58.224
Well, anyway,
as a cleaner of the En Family,

00:58.975 --> 01:00.852
I'm going to

01:02.020 --> 01:03.646
kill you all!

01:06.733 --> 01:07.650
Dokuga!

01:16.534 --> 01:17.452
Ton!

01:17.535 --> 01:19.204
That Noi.

01:19.287 --> 01:22.957
I told her so often
to be careful of their attacks.

01:23.541 --> 01:25.960
- Oh no! His magic!
- I'll seal it before he uses it!

01:28.296 --> 01:32.300
Dodging is easy
if I know where you're aiming.

01:41.559 --> 01:44.479
Hurry and escape through here!

01:44.562 --> 01:46.356
- Hey, Ton!
- One more time.

01:46.439 --> 01:47.482
Idiots.

01:54.864 --> 01:56.116
Ton! Saji!

02:01.830 --> 02:04.624
You revived already? You monster!

02:04.707 --> 02:05.875
Ushishimada!

02:05.959 --> 02:09.337
Natsuki, you go get the boss.

02:10.797 --> 02:12.257
Hurry...

02:14.467 --> 02:15.385
Okay.

02:16.094 --> 02:19.889
Noi, I'll leave the rest to you.
I'll go after the doll.

02:19.973 --> 02:21.224
Roger that!

02:21.307 --> 02:24.144
Put the dismembered ones in a bag.

02:24.227 --> 02:25.228
What?

02:30.733 --> 02:31.860
What the...

02:37.365 --> 02:39.450
There's no one here.

02:40.618 --> 02:41.911
Are they out?

02:46.583 --> 02:48.459
En...

02:53.840 --> 02:55.842
What's this?

02:55.925 --> 02:57.510
A hole in his head?

03:35.632 --> 03:38.676
Aren't you quite a hard worker?

03:46.351 --> 03:48.937
Come on, what's wrong?

03:58.071 --> 03:59.864
You're starting to slow down.

04:02.367 --> 04:04.661
Shall we end this?

04:06.287 --> 04:07.163
Dokuga!

04:07.247 --> 04:08.289
Use this!

04:09.999 --> 04:11.084
What is it?

04:13.878 --> 04:15.546
I said we'd already end it.

04:20.051 --> 04:21.219
Boss...

04:24.597 --> 04:26.724
These guys do futile things.

04:26.808 --> 04:29.310
Dokuga!

04:33.606 --> 04:36.025
Will everyone be okay?

04:36.109 --> 04:38.236
I need to find the boss quickly!

04:49.414 --> 04:51.874
Is he the boss?

04:56.045 --> 04:57.797
What? En?

04:59.924 --> 05:01.843
Stop it!

05:08.808 --> 05:11.019
There's so much blood! What should I do?

05:12.478 --> 05:16.649
Could it be that this person
performed surgery on himself?

05:17.400 --> 05:19.152
What should I do?

05:19.736 --> 05:21.112
At this rate...

05:23.906 --> 05:28.244
Haru, do you really know
where Shin and the others are?

05:28.328 --> 05:29.537
Yeah, easy-peasy.

05:29.620 --> 05:33.583
However, it's boring. I don't care at all.

05:34.375 --> 05:36.044
We're here.

05:36.127 --> 05:41.049
The leader of the Cross-Eyes...
Is that you, Ai?

05:41.132 --> 05:43.051
HEALING A+

05:48.264 --> 05:52.685
The crosses on his eyes
are not tattoos like ours.

05:53.311 --> 05:54.771
They're like birthmarks.

05:58.274 --> 05:59.442
Whoa.

06:02.028 --> 06:05.698
Excuse me, my name is Natsuki.

06:05.782 --> 06:07.825
Nice to meet...

06:10.578 --> 06:12.705
My name is...

06:17.251 --> 06:18.461
Kai.

06:20.046 --> 06:23.216
Noi, are you done over there?

06:23.299 --> 06:25.218
Yeah, I'm all done!

06:25.301 --> 06:29.097
This one wasn't dismembered,
so I just put him directly in a bag.

06:29.180 --> 06:30.348
Guess that's fine.

06:30.932 --> 06:34.060
Shin, we're not going to kill these guys?

06:34.143 --> 06:36.229
We can kill them any time.

06:36.312 --> 06:39.565
But there are so many things
I want to ask them.

06:40.274 --> 06:41.859
Hey, where's the doll?

06:43.945 --> 06:46.864
This is just like six years ago.

06:47.824 --> 06:49.617
This feeling is like

06:50.952 --> 06:52.078
the Hole.

06:53.246 --> 06:54.080
What?

06:54.163 --> 06:56.082
Smoke? Magic?

06:59.085 --> 07:00.586
Impossible!

07:01.254 --> 07:03.214
This is En's...

07:14.267 --> 07:15.726
I see.

07:16.394 --> 07:17.728
It's you.

07:18.813 --> 07:20.022
You're...

07:35.997 --> 07:37.790
I found you.

07:45.006 --> 07:48.009
Wow, this place is a mess.

07:48.092 --> 07:49.302
Yeah!

07:49.385 --> 07:51.012
What is it, Haru?

07:51.095 --> 07:54.765
I just thought of a great song.
Listen to it.

07:54.849 --> 07:56.017
Right now?

07:56.726 --> 08:01.397
This time for sure,
I will take everything from you.

08:01.481 --> 08:04.942
Just like you took my life.

08:07.987 --> 08:11.032
Blood dripping on the wall, so dirty

08:11.115 --> 08:12.909
Why come to a dump like this?

08:12.992 --> 08:13.951
I want to go home

08:14.035 --> 08:17.163
Don't sing this kind of stuff.
Just tell me directly.

08:18.873 --> 08:19.916
A Devil's song!

08:26.672 --> 08:27.590
Hey.

08:27.673 --> 08:31.093
What's wrong, Hayes? Did you fall asleep?

08:31.177 --> 08:32.845
Shocking.

08:33.513 --> 08:35.181
Then, let's go home.

08:48.694 --> 08:50.363
Boss.

08:53.950 --> 08:55.243
Take this.

09:06.796 --> 09:08.089
One month later,

09:09.048 --> 09:11.217
the En Family was destroyed.

10:39.889 --> 10:41.974
THE BEGINNING

10:42.058 --> 10:44.477
CROSS-EYES IN THE NEWS

10:44.560 --> 10:46.479
Fukuyama!

10:46.562 --> 10:49.231
"One month after En's murder,

10:49.315 --> 10:52.860
his huge mansion has been taken over
by the Cross-Eyes."

10:52.943 --> 10:58.282
"After losing their great boss,
the En family has weakened rapidly,

10:58.366 --> 11:02.578
with their members,
including the servants, scattering."

11:03.162 --> 11:05.623
- Go back to work, you idiot!
- Ouch!

11:05.706 --> 11:09.210
But you're curious too, aren't you, boss?

11:09.293 --> 11:13.255
We were selling pie there
until just recently.

11:13.339 --> 11:15.966
That's what makes it even more upsetting.

11:16.050 --> 11:19.428
Just when our wagon business
was going so well.

11:20.012 --> 11:24.016
Speaking of the Cross-Eyes,
I wonder what happened to Caiman.

11:24.100 --> 11:24.934
Well...

11:25.559 --> 11:29.355
It's him we're talking about,
so he's probably alive somewhere.

11:43.703 --> 11:45.496
Hey, Dokuga!

11:46.038 --> 11:48.541
What are you doing in a place like this?

11:49.542 --> 11:52.586
I brought the stuff the boss asked me to,

11:53.087 --> 11:55.047
but he won't let me in.

11:55.548 --> 11:57.550
The boss is in this room?

11:57.633 --> 12:03.723
Yeah. We're not supposed to disturb him
when he's doing something alone.

12:04.598 --> 12:06.267
What are you doing, Natsuki?

12:06.350 --> 12:11.105
Saji asked me to gather
all the valuables in the mansion.

12:11.188 --> 12:13.357
But there's still a lot left.

12:13.441 --> 12:14.942
That much?

12:15.025 --> 12:15.860
Dokuga.

12:15.943 --> 12:19.113
The Cross-Eyes are rich now.
Rolling in cash!

12:20.197 --> 12:21.157
Rich?

12:21.240 --> 12:22.575
Hey, Dokuga!

12:23.075 --> 12:24.994
Here's the additional stuff.

12:25.077 --> 12:29.498
But this mansion is too big.
We need a map.

12:29.582 --> 12:33.627
Ushishimada, Saji, are you done cleaning?

12:33.711 --> 12:34.754
Not at all.

12:35.379 --> 12:40.092
The bodies of En's underlings
who resisted when we took over the place

12:40.176 --> 12:42.011
are still lying around.

12:42.094 --> 12:44.388
What's inside this box?

12:44.472 --> 12:47.349
- What? You want to see?
- Yes.

12:48.559 --> 12:51.979
I was just checking each of these bodies,

12:52.062 --> 12:54.982
but I didn't see any of the top brass.

12:55.065 --> 12:57.902
The two Cleaners are missing too.

12:57.985 --> 12:59.945
But the boss is invincible now.

13:00.029 --> 13:01.238
It's not a big deal.

13:01.322 --> 13:04.909
Oh, yeah! I found something amazing!

13:04.992 --> 13:06.076
It's in that room.

13:08.078 --> 13:09.747
Gold bars!

13:10.623 --> 13:13.626
What's wrong? You don't seem very excited.

13:13.709 --> 13:16.754
Hey, I found something amazing!

13:18.714 --> 13:21.383
A huge stock of daily necessities!

13:21.467 --> 13:23.010
- Wow!
- That's amazing!

13:24.595 --> 13:26.639
So this is what being rich is like.

13:26.722 --> 13:29.350
Hey! Isn't your reaction weird?

13:30.142 --> 13:32.812
What on earth is this?

13:32.895 --> 13:35.272
It's the door that leads to the Hole.

13:36.398 --> 13:39.193
Used by people
who can't make doors with magic.

13:39.276 --> 13:41.028
So this is...

13:42.613 --> 13:44.532
MUSHROOM

13:45.157 --> 13:48.118
Mushrooms!

13:48.202 --> 13:49.286
Is it morning?

13:50.204 --> 13:51.539
That damn clock.

13:51.622 --> 13:53.290
This is damn annoying.

13:53.791 --> 13:57.086
But I can't throw away something
that still works.

13:57.169 --> 13:59.547
Dokuga! Come here, it's an emergency!

14:00.172 --> 14:02.258
Right now, outside the mansion gate.

14:03.133 --> 14:04.677
Let me in!

14:04.760 --> 14:06.220
Let me see the boss!

14:06.303 --> 14:08.848
You've got to be kidding. So suddenly?

14:08.931 --> 14:11.183
What a bunch of opportunists.

14:11.267 --> 14:13.811
Either way, we need to talk to the boss.

14:13.894 --> 14:18.399
I thought so too, and I looked for him,
but he's nowhere to be found.

14:18.482 --> 14:20.067
Seriously? Again?

14:20.150 --> 14:21.485
What do you mean?

14:22.695 --> 14:23.821
Boss...

14:24.321 --> 14:29.243
People who can't use much magic
are starting to gather at En's mansion.

14:29.326 --> 14:31.245
What is the Cross-Eyes' goal?

14:31.328 --> 14:34.248
And what is the identity
of the Cross-Eyes' boss?

14:38.836 --> 14:40.296
This is ridiculous.

14:40.379 --> 14:42.756
Ma'am, I'll leave the money here.

14:42.840 --> 14:44.258
Thank you!

14:47.177 --> 14:49.179
I've got nothing at all to do.

14:49.263 --> 14:53.726
I wonder if there isn't
anything fun to do. Anything like...

14:55.019 --> 14:57.354
Come on, use some magic.

14:57.438 --> 14:59.440
I can't. I can't use it.

14:59.523 --> 15:03.319
Why not?
You're a student there, aren't you?

15:03.402 --> 15:05.362
Come on, use it.

15:05.446 --> 15:06.739
Please stop it.

15:06.822 --> 15:09.116
Don't get cocky, you piece of trash.

15:09.199 --> 15:12.494
You guys are
just like the people from the Hole.

15:12.578 --> 15:15.497
All right then,
you'll be my practice dummy.

15:16.373 --> 15:18.542
What? Who the hell are--

15:24.381 --> 15:27.301
That was some good exercise
to help digestion.

15:27.384 --> 15:29.887
- Excuse me, you're Aikawa, right?
- What?

15:29.970 --> 15:33.265
It's me! We were
in the same class at Zagan's school.

15:33.349 --> 15:34.642
Really?

15:35.392 --> 15:39.688
That school was shut down by En
a few years ago

15:39.772 --> 15:43.275
because it was a hotbed
for the black powder the Cross-Eyes sold.

15:43.359 --> 15:44.401
Right...

15:44.485 --> 15:47.738
But a new school was built recently.

15:47.821 --> 15:49.323
It's really close by.

15:49.406 --> 15:51.992
ACCEPTING APPLICATIONS
FOR TRIAL ENROLLMENT

15:52.993 --> 15:55.162
- Did you submit your application?
- Yeah.

15:56.038 --> 15:59.083
Isn't this place great? I like it.

15:59.166 --> 16:00.918
But I'm worried.

16:01.001 --> 16:04.338
The Cross-Eyes will be dealing
black powder again for sure.

16:04.421 --> 16:08.092
People just began practicing again
once that stuff disappeared.

16:10.177 --> 16:13.597
Everyone at school
only talks about the Cross-Eyes too.

16:14.181 --> 16:17.601
People are happy
that they destroyed the En family.

16:17.685 --> 16:20.354
By the way, how's Risu doing?

16:21.438 --> 16:24.108
Well, I don't know.

16:24.191 --> 16:27.611
Aikawa, I'll treat you to something
at the cafeteria.

16:27.695 --> 16:29.029
Cool!

16:33.909 --> 16:35.577
You bastard, Aikawa!

16:35.661 --> 16:38.163
You work at this school too, old man?

16:38.247 --> 16:40.833
You bastard! Don't come to school!

16:40.916 --> 16:43.085
Bye-bye! See you tomorrow!

16:43.168 --> 16:44.461
See you tomorrow!

16:44.545 --> 16:48.590
Do I really have to start guarding
the school lunches from him again?

16:49.633 --> 16:52.720
Now, what should I do today?

16:59.601 --> 17:02.187
It's also been a while since I came here.

17:03.689 --> 17:06.442
Risu. Hey, are you there?

17:13.949 --> 17:17.828
Ton, are we going to accept those people
into the Cross-Eyes?

17:17.911 --> 17:19.038
Maybe yes.

17:19.121 --> 17:23.500
But aren't they just after money?

17:23.584 --> 17:28.422
Probably yes.
But we've been using people like them.

17:29.006 --> 17:32.926
We pay them for work,
then rule them through fear of the boss.

17:33.010 --> 17:36.513
But if we let them into the mansion,

17:36.597 --> 17:40.309
there might be some
who could try to assassinate the boss.

17:40.392 --> 17:43.312
I have an idea for that.

17:44.938 --> 17:47.900
I found this the other day.

17:47.983 --> 17:52.279
One of En's businesses
is a magic inspection system.

17:53.113 --> 17:56.200
It can quantify the level of Sorcerers.

17:56.700 --> 17:58.786
If we check them before they enter,

17:59.369 --> 18:01.705
we can tell whether they're assassins.

18:02.331 --> 18:04.917
Please check me too.

18:05.000 --> 18:06.293
Sure!

18:06.376 --> 18:08.629
You'll definitely be disappointed.

18:12.091 --> 18:15.719
What is this black liquid?

18:15.803 --> 18:19.389
That liquid's been
in the boss's room for a long time.

18:19.473 --> 18:22.643
And where did the boss go?

18:23.143 --> 18:24.812
Gone for a long time again?

18:24.895 --> 18:27.940
That won't happen.
This is different from that time.

18:28.524 --> 18:31.944
Seriously, Dokuga.
Could you just tell me already?

18:32.027 --> 18:34.696
Just what happened to the boss back then?

18:37.074 --> 18:39.701
Promise not to tell the others?

18:40.452 --> 18:42.788
Sure. But why?

18:43.455 --> 18:49.002
The boss found someone with special magic,
and he wanted that magic.

18:49.503 --> 18:50.337
That was Risu.

18:50.420 --> 18:52.631
I see. It's Curse-type!

18:52.714 --> 18:53.549
Right.

18:53.632 --> 18:55.926
Risu's magic is Curse-type.

18:56.593 --> 18:59.304
It befalls the one who kills him.

18:59.972 --> 19:04.351
The deal is at 4:00 p.m. today
at the ruins in the Salmanazar Field.

19:04.935 --> 19:07.980
Can I bring my partner with me, as usual?

19:08.063 --> 19:11.066
He's not a member of the team,
but I trust him.

19:11.150 --> 19:14.820
No, you can't. You must go alone.

19:18.407 --> 19:21.577
Is this okay, Dokuga?

19:21.660 --> 19:24.496
That's Risu? I've never seen him before.

19:24.580 --> 19:27.791
Is it okay to trust him?
This is an important deal.

19:27.875 --> 19:28.709
It's fine.

19:30.377 --> 19:31.962
Who's that guy with Risu?

19:32.045 --> 19:35.090
He's Risu's partner. His name is Aikawa.

19:35.174 --> 19:36.967
They always hang out together.

19:38.802 --> 19:40.095
Aikawa...

19:41.346 --> 19:45.726
After that, Risu was probably killed
by the boss at the Salmanazar Field.

19:45.809 --> 19:49.062
So the boss was cursed after killing Risu?

19:49.980 --> 19:53.525
Why did you keep
such an important thing a secret?

19:55.110 --> 19:57.738
I thought it was better
if everyone didn't know.

19:58.238 --> 20:03.911
That the boss could kill
a Cross-Eyes member without hesitation.

20:03.994 --> 20:08.624
But we need the boss to survive, right?

20:08.707 --> 20:09.541
Tetsujo.

20:11.960 --> 20:16.965
We, too, might be using the boss,
in a way.

20:19.384 --> 20:21.803
Who killed me?

20:22.888 --> 20:25.265
Why did you kill me?

20:25.349 --> 20:27.893
You are not a Sorcerer.

20:29.019 --> 20:30.812
You are a fake.

20:32.397 --> 20:35.067
Why? Why was I killed?

20:36.860 --> 20:40.072
Why do you ask? You should already know.

20:40.155 --> 20:42.950
Who knows about this magic?

20:43.033 --> 20:44.701
No way! I mean...

20:45.369 --> 20:46.203
Hey!

20:46.787 --> 20:51.750
I bought that self-magic testing machine
we talked about the other day.

20:51.833 --> 20:53.418
The one from En's brand.

20:53.502 --> 20:56.838
And I found out something amazing.

20:56.922 --> 21:00.884
It's not confirmed yet,
but I'll tell only you.

21:05.264 --> 21:06.265
Risu!

21:06.765 --> 21:09.142
Risu, do you recognize me?

21:09.226 --> 21:13.397
It's me, Aikawa. Your partner.

21:13.480 --> 21:15.816
I know, Aikawa.

21:15.899 --> 21:17.943
There's no way I'd forget you.

21:18.568 --> 21:21.530
What the hell happened to you?

21:21.613 --> 21:23.740
Looks like you've been through hell.

21:23.824 --> 21:26.076
It's okay. I'm here for you.

21:26.159 --> 21:28.328
Let's go to school together again.

21:28.412 --> 21:29.538
Okay?

21:31.415 --> 21:35.585
Oh, yeah! Are you hungry?
I'll get you something to eat.

21:35.669 --> 21:37.838
Thank you, Aikawa.

21:37.921 --> 21:39.423
Don't mention it.

21:53.937 --> 21:56.857
Where am I? What's going on?

21:56.940 --> 21:58.984
I remember the Cross-Eyes...

21:59.651 --> 22:00.610
Shin!

22:00.694 --> 22:02.946
So you finally woke up.

22:03.947 --> 22:08.368
It took you unusually long
to recover, Noi.

22:08.952 --> 22:11.121
It's been a month since then.

22:12.080 --> 22:13.623
You're...

22:15.917 --> 22:18.378
- Who are you?
- What? It's me!

22:18.462 --> 22:23.383
A member of the En family!
A Sorcerer who makes anything invisible!

22:24.426 --> 22:25.635
I'm Sho!

22:25.719 --> 22:27.387
Oh, Sho!

22:28.096 --> 22:32.184
I went on a journey for a while
after the Blue Night Festival.

22:32.267 --> 22:34.144
When I heard En was dead,

22:34.227 --> 22:38.940
I secretly returned to the mansion
and watched over all of you.

22:39.024 --> 22:42.319
You stayed invisible with your magic? Why?

22:42.402 --> 22:46.281
Because it seemed like everyone
had completely forgotten about me.

22:47.324 --> 22:50.911
I used to work as an assassin
for the En family,

22:50.994 --> 22:53.663
but my magic may have dulled my presence.

22:53.747 --> 22:58.085
It was common for everyone except En
to completely forget about me.

22:58.168 --> 23:00.379
I was at the Blue Night Festival too.

23:02.339 --> 23:04.841
You were, right?
You were definitely there!

23:04.925 --> 23:08.261
I see! So you were the one who saved me.

23:08.345 --> 23:10.138
More importantly, where's Shin?

23:10.222 --> 23:12.140
Please put on some clothes.

23:12.724 --> 23:16.520
But Shin is probably already...

23:16.603 --> 23:17.771
What?

23:23.693 --> 23:25.362
Shin...

23:25.862 --> 23:31.034
I tried to use some kind of healing-type
smoke to bring Shin back to normal,

23:31.118 --> 23:34.413
but it took all my effort
just to keep the mushrooms fresh.

23:34.913 --> 23:35.914
Huh? Noi!

23:35.997 --> 23:38.917
What are you doing?
You're still recovering.

23:39.000 --> 23:43.422
Besides, the Cross-Eyes boss's magic
is different from En's.

23:45.257 --> 23:46.425
Whoa!

23:46.508 --> 23:50.929
There's no way
I'm going to lose to that bastard's magic.

23:55.809 --> 23:57.894
What an incredible smoke density!

24:16.913 --> 24:19.332
What are you doing?

24:19.416 --> 24:23.086
Shin, thank goodness!

24:23.170 --> 24:24.921
I'm so glad!

24:31.011 --> 24:33.305
Thanks, Noi.

24:34.014 --> 24:38.477
All right, they're already
forgetting that I exist.

24:39.144 --> 24:41.104
Maybe I should just disappear.

26:14.698 --> 26:15.907
THE END

26:15.991 --> 26:18.201
What we learned in Episode 9.

26:18.285 --> 26:20.662
Shin's serious mode
is the forward-facing mask.

26:20.745 --> 26:22.789
The Cross-Eyes' dream
is finally fulfilled.

26:22.872 --> 26:24.541
Aikawa and Risu reunited.

26:24.624 --> 26:29.129
What we'll learn in Episode 10
is still hidden in chaos.

26:29.212 --> 26:30.922
This is Dorohedoro.
